{
	"name": "Airtable content table to sprkly, with approval",
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "bd435f0f-0804-49f9-be9f-773db287dcfb",
			"name": "Overview",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				-1000,
				-80
			],
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Airtable to sprkly, with your OK first\n\n### How it works\n- Every 15 minutes it finds the records with Status **Ready**.\n- A file in the Media field goes to sprkly first. Airtable file links stop working after a few hours, so sprkly keeps its own copy.\n- Each record becomes a post in sprkly that waits for your OK. The Approval Note goes with it.\n- External ID `airtable-<record id>` means a re-run never posts twice.\n- The record gets back its Status, sprkly Post ID, time and any error.\n- When a post goes out, the record gets **Published** and the link. When it fails, **Failed** and the reason.\n\n### Setup\n- Needs the n8n-nodes-sprkly community node (Settings, Community Nodes). More: https://github.com/ahlanlhw/n8n-nodes-sprkly\n- Add your sprkly API key to the 4 sprkly nodes. API docs: https://sprkly.app/docs/api\n- Add your Airtable login to the 3 Airtable nodes, and pick your base and table in each.\n- Fields: Caption, Publish Time, Accounts, Media, Media URL, Approval Note, Status, sprkly Post ID, Scheduled For, Link, Error.\n- Accounts looks like `instagram:clienthandle, telegram:Client channel`. A lookup from a Clients table works too.\n- Give Publish Time a time, not only a date.\n\n### Customize\n- Change how often it runs in **Every 15 minutes**.\n- To skip the OK step, turn off Requires Approval in **Schedule post for approval**.",
				"height": 820,
				"width": 520,
				"color": 1
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "0cb91997-e664-4992-9dbf-968fe3595e02",
			"name": "Note: schedule records",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				-440,
				80
			],
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Schedule Ready records\nOnly the first file in Media is used. A bad file link writes Error to the record and skips the post. Every other record still goes.",
				"height": 500,
				"width": 1460,
				"color": 7
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "186a0a5a-932d-4f33-bfd1-5e1f4e09ef00",
			"name": "Note: track posts",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				-440,
				680
			],
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Track what happened\nWhen a post goes out or fails, the record is found by its id. Only posts with an External ID that starts with airtable- reach this table.",
				"height": 440,
				"width": 760,
				"color": 7
			}
		},
		{
